ruleThisT -- SEQ 397 / 400 / 401 (Tony, 2026-10-22): `$$this;` in a RULE's code. A rule's code locals are minted into
its CodE (the one under builtinActoR), so SEQ 401 gives that CodE `this` -- holding the CodE -- and `tempField`, as an
action's `this` holds the action. rtRule declares two locals and dumps `this`: the dump lists rtFirst and rtSecond by
name. rtInvoke is tester's InvokeR shape. rtAct is the control: an action's `this` already lists its locals. Before SEQ
401 both rule bodies refused `$$` (`this` resolved to the keyword) and `ERROR processCode: ... parse failed`, so neither
ran. The top-level case lives in ruleThisTopT, because its refusal abandons the rest of its file.
